# Component File Structure

Every reusable component under `web/components/primitives/` and `web/components/modals/` lives in its own PascalCase folder with exactly two files:

- `index.tsx` — all component logic, state, and JSX (default export)
- `styles.css` — all styles for that component (layout, surfaces, and component-specific chrome), imported inside `index.tsx`

```
// ❌ BAD — separate component file + re-export barrel
web/components/primitives/Button/
  Button.tsx       ← logic
  index.ts         ← export { default } from "./Button"
  styles.css

// ❌ BAD — shared semiglobal stylesheet for multiple components
web/components/primitives/styles.css

// ✅ GOOD — logic and styles colocated per component
web/components/primitives/Button/
  index.tsx        ← logic + JSX, default export
  styles.css       ← button chrome + any Button-only layout
```

Import by folder path:

```tsx
import Button from "@/components/primitives/Button";
import AuthModal from "@/components/modals/AuthModal";
```

## Styling ownership

- **No** shared `web/components/primitives/styles.css`.
- Button styles → `Button/styles.css`. Badge styles → `Badge/styles.css`. Nav link styles → `NavBar/styles.css`. And so on.
- Design tokens and default `h1`–`h6` / `body` rules → [`web/app/globals.css`](web/app/globals.css) only.

Follow [ui-primitives-first.mdc](ui-primitives-first.mdc) for tokens, semantic tags, and styling priority.

## Modals

Modal components follow the same folder pattern. See also [modal-structure.mdc](modal-structure.mdc).
